  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ramprakash Bhutra vs State Of Rajasthan on 2 August, 2019 Author: Dinesh Mehta Bench: Dinesh Mehta High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan At Jodhpur S.B. Civil Writ Petition No. 11419/2019 Ramprakash Bhutra S/o Pukhraj Bhutra, Aged About 62 Years, By Caste Maheshwari, (Seller And Owner) M/s Maheshwari Trading Company, Main Market, Raipur, District Pali (Rajasthan). ----Petitioner Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan, Through Food Safety Commissioner, Rajasthan, Jaipur. 2. Anand Kumar, Food Safety Officer, Office Of Chief Medical And Health Officer, Pali (Raj.). ----Respondents For Petitioner(s) : Mr. D.D. Chitlangi Justice Dinesh Mehta Order 02/08/2019",
    "facts": "The present writ petition is directed against the order dated 26.04.2019, passed by the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal, Jaipur in an appeal, filed by the petitioner against the order dated 06.11.2017, passed by the Prescribed Authority and Additional District Magistrate, Pali. The facts in brief, are that the petitioner Proprietor of M/s. Maheshwari Trading Company deals in oil and other miscellaneous provisions. In pursuance of a survey, conducted at his shop on 20.07.2015, a sample of groundnut oil was drawn by respondent No.2, which was found to be substandard. The petitioner himself moved an application under Section 26(2)(2) of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 (hereinafter referred to as 'the Act of 2006') for compounding, for (2 of 3) [CW-11419/2019] which a penalty to the tune of Rs.1,50,000/- under Section 52 of the Act of 2006 was imposed upon him, by order dated 06.11.2017 by the Prescribed Authority. The petitioner preferred an appeal against the said order, before the Food Safety Appellate Tribunal, Jaipur, which has been rejected by the Tribunal, vide its order dated 26.04.2019.",
    "arguments": "Neither before the authority concerned nor before the Appellate Authority, the petitioner has pointed as to how determination of penalty of Rs.1,50,000/- was erroneous. Mr. Chitlangi, learned counsel for the petitioner, however, invited attention of the Court towards invoice of M/s. Ghisulal Udhyog, the manufacturer of the concerned groundnut oil (3 of 3) [CW-11419/2019] and prayed that the penalty, as a matter of fact, ought to have been imposed upon the manufacturer.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Neither before the authority concerned nor before the Appellate Authority, the petitioner has pointed as to how determination of penalty of Rs.1,50,000/- was erroneous. Mr. Chitlangi, learned counsel for the petitioner, however, invited attention of the Court towards invoice of M/s. Ghisulal Udhyog, the manufacturer of the concerned groundnut oil (3 of 3) [CW-11419/2019] and prayed that the penalty, as a matter of fact, ought to have been imposed upon the manufacturer.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
